\details{
\subsection{MSY Reference Points}{

Calculated by \code{\link[=CalcMSY]{CalcMSY()}} and stored in \code{Hist@Reference@MSY}.
\itemize{
\item \code{MSYRefs()}, \code{MSY()}: the full \link[=refpointsMSY-class]{refpointsMSY} object.
\item \code{FMSY()}: apical fishing mortality at MSY, defined at the complex
level.
\item \code{BMSY()}: total biomass at MSY.
\item \code{SBMSY()}: spawning biomass at MSY.
\item \code{SPMSY()}: spawning production at MSY.
\item \code{SPRMSY()}: spawning potential ratio at MSY.
\item \code{MSYLandings()}: landed catch at MSY.
\item \code{MSYDiscards()}: dead discards at MSY.
}

The replacement functions (e.g. \verb{FMSY<-}) set the reference points of a
\link[=refpointsMSY-class]{refpointsMSY} or \link[=referencedata-class]{referencedata} object, such as the
\code{Reference} slot of a \link[=data-class]{data} object. The reference points of a
\link[=hist-class]{hist} or \link[=mse-class]{mse} object are calculated by \code{\link[=Simulate]{Simulate()}} and
cannot be replaced.
}

\subsection{Per-Recruit and Replacement-Line Reference Points}{

Calculated by \code{\link[=CalcRefPoints]{CalcRefPoints()}} and stored in \code{Hist@Reference}.
\itemize{
\item \code{F01()}: apical F at 10\% of the complex's yield-per-recruit slope at the
origin.
\item \code{FMax()}: apical F maximising the complex's yield-per-recruit.
\item \code{FSPR()}: apical F at each requested SPR target.
\item \code{FMed()}: apical F at the median historical replacement line.
\item \code{FCrash()}: apical F at which the stock can no longer replace itself.
\item \code{SPRcrash()}: spawning potential ratio at \code{FCrash()}.
\item \code{BLow()}: spawning biomass rebuilding threshold (see \code{\link[=CalcBLow]{CalcBLow()}}).
Only populated when computed explicitly, since it is substantially
more expensive than the other reference points here.
\item \code{SPR0()}: unfished spawning potential ratio (spawning production per
recruit).
\item \code{MGT()}: mean generation time (see \code{\link[=CalcMGT]{CalcMGT()}}).
}

\code{\link[=Landings]{Landings()}} and \code{\link[=Removals]{Removals()}} return the \code{Landings} and \code{Removals} slots
of a \link[=reference-class]{reference} object.
}

\subsection{Unfished Reference Points}{

Stored in \code{Hist@Unfished}.
\itemize{
\item \code{B0()}: total biomass.
\item \code{SB0()}: spawning biomass.
\item \code{SP0()}: spawning production.
\item \code{N0()}: numbers-at-age.
}
}
}
